   [
    0.1,
    "Start with one chain."
   ],
   [
    1.599,
    "Along it are stretches of helix, stretches of sheet, and loops in between."
   ],
   [
    6.3,
    "The chain bends and packs these pieces into one compact, three-dimensional shape."
   ],
   [
    11.3,
    "The final shape of a single chain is its tertiary structure."
   ],
   [
    14.881,
    "Your slide calls this folded shape a domain."
   ],
   [
    17.55,
    "Strictly, a domain is a compact region inside it, and a long chain may fold into several."
   ],
   [
    23.618,
    "The key point is the same either way."
   ],
   [
    25.844,
    "The shape decides the function, and if the shape is disrupted, the protein loses its activity."
   ]
